{
  "run_id": "PMC10920630__problem_constrained__web_agent_o3mini__s1",
  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The study material is uncoated Q235 steel with its native microstructure and surface finish.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Formation and integrity of a spontaneous iron oxide/hydroxide passivation film govern corrosion-related degradation of uncoated Q235 steel.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427115::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At room temperature, gradual formation of a uniform passivation layer slows corrosion onset.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated temperature accelerates passivation-film growth.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, chloride attack causes breakdown of the passivation film and produces pitting corrosion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427115::page::001",
        "PMC7287792::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant structural mediator is the integrity and continuity of a spontaneously formed iron oxide/hydroxide surface layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427115::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed passivation layer consists predominantly of Fe2O3 and FeOOH.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slower room-temperature reaction kinetics favor development of a relatively uniform, protective film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A relatively uniform passivation film retards subsequent corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427115::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, thermal stresses destabilize the passivation film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "At elevated temperature, increased chloride-ion mobility promotes localized film breakdown and pitting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427115::page::001",
        "PMC7287792::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Room-temperature samples will have lower corrosion current density than samples tested at 60–80°C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Room-temperature samples will have fewer localized pitting events than samples tested at 60–80°C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature samples will exhibit significantly higher corrosion rates because of passivation-film degradation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Elevated-temperature samples will exhibit pronounced pitting.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6427115::page::001",
        "PMC7287792::page::001"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Q235 steel maintained in a neutral, non-corrosive environment will undergo negligible corrosion.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface roughness, prior atmospheric exposure, chloride concentration, and pH can influence passivation-film formation and corrosion behavior.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A lack of significant temperature-dependent differences in corrosion current, pitting potential, and film integrity would falsify the proposed temperature-driven film-instability mechanism.",
